# Move descriptions for the move menu (<= 44 chars, ASCII).
[desc.chirp]
A tiny radio peep. Weak but cheap.
A cheap peep. Every Chirplet knows it.
Small NORM hit that costs almost no EN.

[desc.static_snap]
A sharp VOLT crackle. Great vs DATA.
Snaps built-up static at the foe.
VOLT jolt. Bugs and lag hate it.

[desc.echo_pulse]
A NET wave that bounces back louder.
Bouncing NET wave. Nothing in VOID.
Echoing NET hit. Good vs VOLT.

[desc.bright_arc]
A hot FIRE arc. Melts DATA and NET.
Big FIRE arc. Less accurate.
Searing light. Firewalls ignore it.

[desc.stray_handshake]
A borrowed NET greeting packet.
NET hit learned from a nearby device.
Friendly packet, unfriendly impact.

[desc.packet_burst]
A rushed DATA spray. Shreds VOID.
Big DATA burst. Kernel panics hate it.
Spray of DATA borrowed from a beacon.

[desc.noise_veil]
VOID hiss. Halves the next hit taken.
Guard: the next hit does half damage.
Hide in static. Halves the next hit.

[desc.signal_sniff]
A curious DATA sniff. Good vs VOID.
Cheap DATA poke that finds glitches.
Sniffs out VOID things. Low cost.

[desc.beacon_burst]
A bright FIRE pop from a loud AP.
FIRE pop. Burns spam and viruses.
Hot beacon flash. Good vs NET.

[desc.channel_hop]
A quick NET skip across channels.
Hops channels to hit from the side.
NET hit. Does nothing to VOID.

[desc.blue_pulse]
A soft ICE pulse. Cools FIRE down.
Cold blue pulse. Freezes worms.
ICE hit learned from Bluetooth.

[desc.tooth_echo]
An icy echo of a Bluetooth handshake.
ICE echo. Great vs firewalls.
Chilly echo that slows NET foes.

[desc.ping_echo]
A bounced DATA ping. Very accurate.
DATA ping that rarely misses.
Cheap DATA hit. Good vs VOID.

[desc.arp_whisper]
A VOID murmur from the local net.
Spooky VOID whisper. Hurts NORM.
Quiet VOID hit. Weak vs DATA foes.

[desc.tag_bite]
A sharp VOLT nibble from an RFID tag.
